  "narrative": "This wave mostly confirms earlier strong associations and identifies one new strong association. H20 and H21 show that the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 and MSI-high/WRN effects remain very large and precise within adenocarcinoma. H35 and H36 show the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 and KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 effects remain essentially unchanged when restricted to the dominant Avana screen library. These are accepted as dataset-level robustness confirmations; they do not establish causality or generalizability beyond this dataset. H14, H16, H42, and H43 do not support clinically meaningful stronger dependency: the point estimates are near zero or opposite, and the maximum claimed-direction interval support is below the approximate 10% relative-scale threshold for these outcomes, so they are rejected and closed. H22 is an ARID1A co-loss interaction on the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association; the point estimate is in the hypothesized direction but is small and imprecise, so it is unresolved and deferred rather than accepted. H37 is near null for BRCA2 loss and WRN dependency; although its wide interval includes some clinically meaningful negative values, the point estimate is essentially zero, so it is unresolved and closed. H39 is borderline: the signed estimate suggests MSI-high may have stronger USP7 dependency and the point estimate is plausibly meaningful, but the interval crosses null and could be confounded by p53 status, mutation burden, or screening context; it remains unresolved and active. H15 is the main new finding: TP53 wild-type versus TP53-loss cells show a raw USP7 dependency difference of about -0.396 (reported signed +0.396), with a narrow interval far above the clinical threshold and biologically plausible because wild-type p53 pathway states may increase USP7 dependency. I accept H15 and request independent validation because it is a new, large, pathway-level association and independent confirmation would be scientifically useful. Multiplicity and confounding remain concerns: these are unadjusted Welch comparisons in a cross-sectional cell-line dataset, and predictors may correlate with screen library, batch, growth pattern, ploidy, or mutation burden. I registered H15 stratification analyses in Avana, adenocarcinoma, and adherent culture, plus a USP7-MSI analysis restricted to TP53 wild-type cells, to test whether the new USP7 effect and the borderline MSI-USP7 signal are robust or confounded.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset associations: H9 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H10 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H13 KEAP1 loss -> higher/weaker NFE2L2 dependency; H15 TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency, active with independent validation requested. H20, H21, H35, and H36 are accepted confirmations of main/robustness contrasts for NFE2L2, WRN, SMARCA2, and screening-library context. Rejected/closed nulls: H14 ARID1A-SMARCA2, H16 TP53-RPL11, H42 marker D-SMARCA2, H43 marker F-WRN. H22 SMARCA4-ARID1A interaction unresolved deferred; H37 BRCA2-WRN unresolved closed; H39 MSI-USP7 unresolved active and borderline. Next priorities: analyze TP53-WT/USP7 robustness in Avana, adenocarcinoma, and adherent culture; analyze USP7-MSI within TP53-WT to assess p53 confounding; await H15 validation and revise interpretation if needed. No causal claims."
}

